BacBench gene-essentiality DNA data — provenance
=================================================

Dataset : macwiatrak/bacbench-essential-genes-dna  (HuggingFace)
Revision: 0210c2445e89c765c0fe5d69618b8a6c262e5d30
License : Apache-2.0
Upstream: Database of Essential Genes (DEG, CC-BY-4.0) + NCBI GenBank/RefSeq (public domain)
Cite    : "BacBench: Evaluating Genomic Language Models for Bacteria" (ICLR 2026 submission).

169,408 genes across 51 bacterial genomes / 37 species, binary essentiality labels. The
genus-disjoint train(37) / validation(9) / test(9) genome splits are the dataset's native
HuggingFace splits.

gLMBench vendors, per split, a compact CSV (genome_name, genus, essential, sequence) where
``sequence`` is the BacBench DNA-LM model input — CDS + 128 bp upstream promoter,
strand-aware, NO reverse complement — extracted once at fetch time by the byte-identical
recipe in ``glmbench.tasks.bacbench_essentiality_data.get_dna_seq`` (recycled from upstream
``bacbench/modeling/embed_dna.py``, commit 64b7d458). The heavy CSVs are gitignored; the
sha256-pinned ``manifest.yaml`` + the committed tiny fixture make the integrity gate real.
